{"This sets the klog context to d.Log instead of the request-scoped logger with name/kind/method values, so downstream storage calls won't inherit the structured fields": 0.9186555743217468, "In the async legacy DeleteCollection path, this records a storage duration metric instead of a legacy duration metric, so the metrics don't reflect which backend was being exercised": 0.9741860628128052, "recordStorageDuration labels are defined as {kind,method} but passing the object name here inflates cardinality and mislabels the metric": 0.7612650394439697, "The legacy Create is invoked in a goroutine using the request object directly, which can cause data races or writing inconsistent data to the legacy store since the apiserver/caller may reuse or mutate that object after the function returns - other modes pass a DeepCopy into async writes": 0.8042037487030029, "The mode-3 tests don't assert that the asynchronous legacy writes actually happen - the test can pass even if the goroutine never runs": 0.8847616910934448, "Both the legacy and unified store mocks share the same underlying mock.Mock, so expectations for Create/Update can be matched by either store, making the tests ambiguous - consider using separate mock instances per store": 0.7481297254562378, "Missing synchronization on the async call (channel/WaitGroup) before asserting expectations in mode-3 tests": 0.7162790894508362, "go.work.sum contains a duplicate entry for github.com/grafana/grafana/pkg/apimachinery v0.0.0-20240701135906-559738ce6ae1/go.mod - consider re-running `go work sync` or removing the duplicate line to keep the sum file stable": 0.88632732629776}